Kat

Thanks for doing such thorough homework prior to sending your questions to the list. That is why past messages are available to search. Let me address your questions in order:
NAs in distdata file. When constructing data files for dsm this is done differently then when organising data for the Distance package. As the distdata name suggests, this data frame contains information about the detection distances. Consequently, it will not contain information about transects without detections.
Staying with the distdata data frame, the Effort column in this data frame will be the length of the transect. The same holds true for the obsdata data frame; Effort is transect length. That is not true for the segdata data frame; Effort there is segment length. obsdata contains information only about observations; therefore there will be no NAs for distance or size.
You are correct that the pantropical dolphin example as presented in our examples vignette depends upon depreciated packages.
we are in the process of updating our examples (more information about that in a month or two). Meanwhile, you can have a glimpse in advance of the pantropical dolphin analysis with those dependencies removed here:
http://distancedevelopment.github.io/dsm/articles/lines_gomex/mexico-analysis.html
Hope that clears up the ambiguity.

